 and good, hard racing.\nToday's race is the second of three held during the Wisconsin State Fair. The first was the 150-mile\nstock car event scheduled for last Sunday. On this Sunday, Aug. 23, the 200 mile, 10th annual Tony\nBettenhausen Classic for championship (Indy) cars,will end the fair. The next stock car race, a 250-mile\nevent, is scheduled for Sunday, Sept. 13. We hope to see you at both.\nShould you have any comments on today's race, please feel free to contact us.\nSincerely,\nJohn Kaishian, Tom Marchese\nCo-Race Directors\nWISCONSIN AUTO RACING, INC.\nThe big, mean \"winged thing,\" a 1970 Plymouth SuperBird, driven by Roger McCluskey to a win\nON THE COVER:\nin July's \"Miller 200.\" McCluskey was the winner of the Thursday 200-mile stock car race here\nlast year.\nCOVER DESIGN: Mike Fabianac, 7016 W. Allerton Ave., Greenfield, Wis.\nRuss Lake, Armin Krueger, Bob Lewis, Al Krause, Paul Gohde, George Kaprelian,\nPHOTOS COURTESY OF:\nMark Thiesen, Gary Schmidt, and Midwest Racing News.\nPage One\n200 MILE STOCK CAR RACE","ocr_json":{"space":"normalized","source":"prepared_image","image_sha256":"10df5ab541b49881fe9faa8e7904e2391f1aac6332ef76e4322f74b4e5e2a5f8","lines":[{"t":"X.","x":0.044167,"y":0.001318,"w":0.008333,"h":0.004614,"s":0.561},{"t":"NINGEST RI","x":0.13125,"y":0.034278,"w":0.241667,"h":0.090969,"s":0.9874},{"t":"Welcome to the","x":0.555417,"y":0.108108,"w":0.142917,"h":0.031641,"s":0.9921},{"t":"200 MILE","x":0.545417,"y":0.158866,"w":0.16375,"h":0.047462,"s":0.9991},{"t":"Late Model","x":0.56625,"y":0.225445,"w":0.122917,"h":0.036256,"s":0.9674},{"t":"Stock Car Race","x":0.54625,"y":0.279499,"w":0.161667,"h":0.036915,"s":0.9983},{"t":"Bob Lewis Photo","x":0.925,"y":0.332235,"w":0.047083,"h":0.011206,"s":0.9768},{"t":"What's behind","x":0.215833,"y":0.345419,"w":0.067083,"h":0.045485,"s":0.9994},{"t":"brands of rings combined.","x":0.274583,"y":0.352011,"w":0.113333,"h":0.033619,"s":0.9778},{"t":"Co-promoters John Kaishian (left) and Tom M